#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:137
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Localsearch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><warning><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:141
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you are upgrading this package from a version where it was known as "
"<application>tracker-miners</application>, there are several files which "
"will cause conflicts. Before installing this package, remove these files as "
"the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:148
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">rm -fv /etc/xdg/autostart/tracker-miner-fs-3.desktop                           &amp;&amp;\n"
"rm -fv /usr/lib/systemd/user/tracker-miner-fs-3.service                        &amp;&amp;\n"
"rm -fv /usr/lib/systemd/user/tracker-miner-fs-control-3.service                &amp;&amp;\n"
"rm -fv /usr/share/dbus-1/services/org.freedesktop.Tracker3.Miner.Files.service &amp;&amp;\n"
"rm -fv /usr/share/dbus-1/services/org.freedesktop.Tracker3.Writeback.service   &amp;&amp;\n"
"rm -fv /usr/share/dbus-1/services/org.freedesktop.Tracker3.Miner.Files.Control.service</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:157
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you plan to run the tests, some timeouts are too short when using "
"spinning disks. There are two places where timeouts are used: first, "
"individual tests inside a group of tests have a default timeout of 10s. This"
" can be changed by setting the environment variable "
"<envar>TRACKER_TESTS_AWAIT_TIMEOUT</envar> to the desired value when running"
" the tests (see below). Second, a global timeout for a group of tests is "
"fixed at configuration time. The default value in the <filename "
"class=\"directory\">functional-tests</filename> directory (other directories"
" have only short lived tests) may be increased with the following command "
"(replace 200 with a value suitable for your machine):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:170
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>sed -i s/120/<replaceable>200</replaceable>/ tests/functional-"
"tests/meson.build</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:183
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>Localsearch</application> by running the following "
"commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:188
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup --prefix=/usr             \\\n"
"            --buildtype=release       \\\n"
"            -D man=false              \\\n"
"            -D functional_tests=false \\\n"
"            ..                        &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:198
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup --prefix=/usr                  \\\n"
"            --buildtype=release            \\\n"
"            -D systemd_user_services=false \\\n"
"            -D man=false                   \\\n"
"            -D functional_tests=false      \\\n"
"            ..                             &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. One test,
#.       <filename>
#. test_cli_inhibit</filename>, is known to fail.
#.       Seem to pass if man pages are built (pierre)
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:210
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To test the results, issue the following commands. Make sure that you adjust"
" the individual test timeout to a value suitable for your machine, please "
"read the note above for more details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:217
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>meson configure -D man=true -D functional_tests=true &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja                                                &amp;&amp;\n"
"dbus-run-session env LC_ALL=C.UTF-8 TRACKER_TESTS_AWAIT_TIMEOUT=<replaceable>20</replaceable> \\\n"
"                 ninja test</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:223
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:226
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>ninja install</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:238
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:244
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D man=false</parameter>: This switch prevents the build process "
"from generating man pages. Omit this switch if you have <xref "
"linkend=\"asciidoc\" role=\"nodep\"/> installed and wish to generate and "
"install the man pages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:251
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D functional_tests=false</parameter>: This switch prevents the "
"setup process to require <xref linkend=\"python-dbusmock\"/> and fail if it "
"is not installed. You can remove this switch if it is installed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:257
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D systemd_user_services=false</parameter>: This switch prevents "
"the build process from installing systemd units since they are useless on "
"SysV systems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:263
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>-D seccomp=false</option>: This option disables the seccomp system "
"call filter. On some architectures, such as ARM, the functions that "
"localsearch uses are not guarded properly, and localsearch will get killed "
"with a SIGSYS signal as a result of this. Note that disabling seccomp may "
"cause the system to be compromised worse in the event that a security "
"vulnerability in localsearch or its dependencies is exploited, and it is "
"<emphasis>NOT</emphasis> recommended."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:273
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>-D landlock=disabled</option>: This switch disables the Landlock "
"file access sandbox.  Use it if you don't want to build the kernel with "
"Landlock support.  Note that disabling Landlock may cause the system to be "
"compromised worse in the event that a security vulnerability in localsearch "
"or its dependencies is exploited, and this is <emphasis>NOT</emphasis> "
"recommended."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:282
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>-D battery_detection=none</option>: Use this option if you have not "
"installed the recommended dependency upower.  Do not use this option if your"
" system has a battery (laptop battery or UPS), or else localsearch may waste"
" battery life when A/C power is unavailable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/localsearch.xml:289
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>-D libav=disabled</option>: Use this option if you have not "
"installed the recommended dependency ffmpeg. Note that using this will cause"
" 7 test failures, and will also significantly hamper the functionality of "
"this package."
msgstr ""

